# Style

How code and words look here. Match the file you are in before you match this
document, and match this document before you match your own habits.

## Words the user reads

Every label, button, error, empty state and heading.

- **No em dashes.** A comma, a full stop or a colon does the job.
- Say what happens next. "Save changes" beats "Submit". "We could not reach the
  server, try again" beats "An error occurred".
- No filler: delve, leverage, seamless, robust, comprehensive, elevate,
  unlock, empower.
- Sentence case for headings and buttons.
- Short. If a sentence can lose a word without losing meaning, it loses the word.
- Write the error and empty states. A default empty screen is an unfinished one.

## Design

Everything here is a rule against looking auto-generated, because looking
auto-generated is what a person notices first and trusts least.

- No purple-to-blue gradient on everything. Pick a palette and mean it.
- No row of three identical feature cards with an icon each.
- No emoji as headings or bullet points.
- No hero section that says nothing. If the first screen does not say what this
  is and what to do, it is decoration.
- Spacing on a scale, not per element. Type on a scale, not per heading.
- One accent colour with a real job. Everything cannot be emphasised.
- Motion under 200ms, and none of it decorative.
- Test it dark and light, and at 360px wide.

