## Code

- {{LANGUAGE_CONVENTIONS}}
- Names say what a thing is. A comment explaining a name is a name that needs
  changing.
- Comments explain why, never what. The code already says what.
- Errors carry what failed and what to do about it.
- No dead code, no commented-out blocks, no `console.log` left behind. Git
  remembers the version you deleted.

## Commits

- Present tense, one line, what changed and why if it is not obvious.
- No em dashes there either.
